menu "JetKVM screen"

choice JETKVM_SCREEN_ROTATION
    prompt "Display hardware rotation"
    default JETKVM_SCREEN_ROTATION_0
    help
        Rotate the ST7789 display in hardware. This changes the controller's
        MADCTL bits and GRAM window; it does not rotate pixels in software.

config JETKVM_SCREEN_ROTATION_0
    bool "0 degrees"

config JETKVM_SCREEN_ROTATION_90
    bool "90 degrees clockwise"

config JETKVM_SCREEN_ROTATION_180
    bool "180 degrees"

config JETKVM_SCREEN_ROTATION_270
    bool "270 degrees clockwise"

endchoice

config JETKVM_SCREEN_BUTTONS
    bool "Drive the local UI with the SW2 and SW3 push buttons"
    default n
    help
        The two push buttons beside the panel navigate the local display.
        The upper button (SW3) goes back; the lower button (SW2) steps down
        or scrolls on a tap and accepts on a hold. The confirmation screens
        keep their hold countdown on the lower button. While this is enabled
        the video component leaves SW3 alone, so the button does not toggle
        the HDMI preview mode.

endmenu
